# SEO (Search Engine Optimization) Rules

> Rules for implementing technical SEO, meta tags, and search optimization

## Core Principles

- SEO is built-in, not bolted-on
- Every page must have unique, descriptive metadata
- Semantic HTML structure is mandatory
- Performance impacts rankings (Core Web Vitals)
- Mobile-first indexing compliance

## Technology Stack

- **Meta Management**: `next-seo` or `next/head`
- **Sitemap**: `next-sitemap`
- **Structured Data**: `schema-dts` + JSON-LD
- **Robots**: `robots.txt` + meta robots tags
- **Performance**: Lighthouse CI in build process

## File Structure

```
├── app/
│   ├── layout.tsx          # Global metadata
│   ├── robots.ts           # Dynamic robots.txt
│   ├── sitemap.ts          # Dynamic sitemap
│   └── [...pages]
├── lib/seo/
│   ├── config.ts           # SEO defaults
│   ├── schema.ts           # Structured data helpers
│   └── utils.ts            # SEO utilities
├── public/
│   └── robots.txt          # Fallback robots
└── next-sitemap.config.js  # Sitemap generation
```

